.idea/
# ⚠️ ANCHORED TO THE REPOSITORY ROOT, and the leading slash is load-bearing.
#
# An unanchored `target/` matches a directory called `target` ANYWHERE, including a Java package —
# and it did: `net.innoventa.tessera.security.access.target` was silently untracked, so three source
# files (`IssueByKey`, `IssueAccessTargetResolver`, `IssueByKeyAccessTargetResolver`) had never been
# committed and a fresh clone did not compile. Nothing reports that; `git status` shows an ignored
# file as nothing at all.
#
# `bin`, `out` and `output` are anchored for the same reason before they cost anybody the same day.
# These four are build outputs of THIS module, which is where they are and the only place they are.
/target/
/bin/
/out/
/output/
.settings/
.vscode/
*.iml
.project
.classpath
.factorypath
.DS_Store

*.private.properties
*sensitive.yml
*public.properties
*.db
